-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/e7402fd3-1b4c-57b3-a4fa-33e4c7140a70
-- title:
--   Affine Drinfeld chart with q+1 nodes forces W₀=𝒪'∩ F₀
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$, and write $\kappa$ for the residue field of $A$. Places are understood in the sense of the project notion `Place K F`: a proper valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$ whose ring is a principal ideal ring, with $\operatorname{ord}$ the associated normalised order function and $\mathrm{evalAt}$ the $K$-valued evaluation obtained by inverting $K\to$ residue field on the residue of an element of the ring (and $0$ off the ring).
--
--   The curve data are: `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by the series `jqModC κ` and its $M'$-fold $q$-expansion; a finite set $W$ of places of this field, which the hypothesis `hW` requires to consist exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' κ`, that is those places $w$ which are rational, lie in `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M'`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at the generator `jGeomGen κ M'` lies in `ssJSet q κ`; `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the $d$-fold $q$-expansions of $j$ for $d\mid M'$; and `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the $X_H$-function field of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   Reduction from characteristic $0$ to $\kappa$ is given by a `ConstantReduction` datum $R_0$ for $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective ring map $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto the level-$M'$ field over $\kappa$ with kernel the maximal ideal, a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places, together with the axioms that constants are integral exactly when they lie in $A$, that the residue map is compatible with reduction of constants, that every nonzero element becomes integral with nonzero residue after scaling by a constant, that degrees of places are preserved and that divisors of integral elements with nonzero residue push forward to divisors of their residues. The hypothesis `hR₀` adds that every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is $R_0$-integral, with $R_0$-residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. An element $s\in W$, i.e. a supersingular place, is fixed.
--
--   The arithmetic of the base is described by: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`); the hypothesis `hκ`, that every $a\in A$ differs from some element of $k_0\cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$; an element $\zeta$ of `Idx q`, the set of primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (the clauses of the conclusion re-quantify over such roots); an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b=\bot$ (`hKb`), a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ whose elements are exactly those mapping into $A$ (`hAb`), and an element $\varpi_b\neq 0$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$ (`hϖb`, `hϖb0`).
--
--   Finally, $\mathcal O'$ is a valuation subring of `fieldBar q M'` subject to three hypotheses. (cst) `hO'_A`: for $x\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the image of $x$ lies in $\mathcal O'$ if and only if $x\in A$. (over) `hO'_over`: for every $f\in$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` which is $R_0$-integral, which is regular wherever $j$ is regular (for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the base-changed `jq` implies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$), and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $\mathcal O'$, and moreover for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in $\mathcal O'$ and in its maximal ideal. (fix) `hO'_fix`: for every $\zeta'\in$ `Idx q` and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, the pullback of $\mathcal O'$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` is $\mathcal O'$.
--
--   The conclusion is formulated for the $k_0$-algebra structure on `fieldBar q M'` obtained by composing $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with the structure map, and asserts the following for all further data.
--
--   Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ satisfying (F-stab): $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for all $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` and all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $F_0$ satisfying (W-cst), that for $x\in k_0$ one has $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $W_0$; (W-dvr), that $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; (W-unif), that $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal; and (W-over), that for every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $R_0$-integral, is regular wherever $j$ is regular in the sense above, and has $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$, lies in $W_0$, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of that image and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$. (Thus (W-over) is imposed only for functions defined over $\mathbb Q$, whereas (over) is imposed for all of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`.)
--
--   Let $B$ be a subring of `fieldBar q M'` with an $A_b$-algebra structure satisfying: (B-alg) the structure map sends $a\in A_b$ to the image of $a\in K_b\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in `fieldBar q M'`; (B-le) every $f\in B$ lies in $F_0$ and, as such, in $W_0$; (B-prime) the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is prime; (B-loc) for $f\in F_0$, $f\in W_0$ if and only if there are $g,h\in B$ with the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$ in $B$ and $f\cdot h=g$; (B-stab) $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for all $\zeta$ and all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; and (B-drinfeld), which requires that for every $(\mathbb F_{q^2})$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $\kappa[x,y]$ by $xy^q-x^qy=1$) is a domain, and every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ C`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32), the fixed field in the Drinfeld function field $\mathrm{Frac}(\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa)$ of the subgroup generated by the $C$-scalar automorphisms, such that: the number of elements of $C$ equals $2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` (the quotient of `jWidthChar q` of the $j$-value of $s$ by `placeRamificationJ M' s`); the kernel of $\rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ composed with the structure map $A_b\to B$ is reduction of $A_b$ to $\kappa$ followed by $\kappa\to$ `quotField`; every $z$ in `quotField` satisfies $z\cdot\rho(h)=\rho(g)$ for some $g,h\in B$ with $\rho(h)\neq 0$; the range of $\rho$ consists exactly of those $z$ whose underlying element of the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$; and for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ such that $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(g,u)\mapsto\det(g)\,u^{q+1}$) and every $f\in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` $f\in B$, the image under $\rho$ of that element equals [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ applied to $\rho(f)$, as elements of the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   Let finally `nodes` be a finite set of subrings of $F_0$ with: (N-count) exactly $q+1$ elements; (N-perm) for every $\zeta$, every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $O\in$ `nodes` there is $O'\in$ `nodes` such that for all $f\in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` $f\in F_0$ one has $f\in O$ if and only if that image lies in $O'$; (N-trans) for every $\zeta$ and all $O,O'\in$ `nodes` there is $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ realising such a correspondence between $O$ and $O'$; (N-sep) for distinct $O,O'\in$ `nodes` there is an element of $O\cap O'$ which is a non-unit of $O$ and a unit of $O'$; and (cover) for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ satisfying the analogues of (W-cst) and (W-over) with $V$ in place of $W_0$, either every $f\in B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $V$, or there is $O\in$ `nodes` such that every $f\in O$ lies in $V$ and, if $f$ is a non-unit of $O$, lies in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   Under all these hypotheses: for every $f\in F_0$, $f\in W_0$ if and only if the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $\mathcal O'$. That is, $W_0$ is the trace of $\mathcal O'$ on $F_0$.
--
--   The statement identifies, at a supersingular place $s$ of $X_0(M')$ over the residue field of $A$, the discrete valuation ring $W_0$ of a $k_0$-form $F_0$ of the full level-$q^2M'$ function field with the trace of the valuation ring $\mathcal O'$ singled out by the conditions on constants, on reductions of level-$M'$ functions regular away from the cusps, and by $\Gamma_0(M')$-invariance; the input is an affine chart $(B,\rho)$ whose special fibre is the Drinfeld curve $xy^q-x^qy=1$ together with a set of $q+1$ node rings covering all remaining valuations. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_nodeChart_point_specializes_iff_adicCompletion_stalk_of_normalModel_gen_j_local`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_nodeChart_point_specializes_iff_adicCompletion_stalk_of_normalModel_gen_j_local) and by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_drinfeldRing_iff_localization_formallySmooth_card_le_descent`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_drinfeldRing_iff_localization_formallySmooth_card_le_descent) in the analysis of the semistable model of the modular curve at a supersingular point.
